          {
            "commit": "dd48e6b096c367e5dfac9bac34641f7691cf9908",
            "subject": "LU-20438 lnet: Implement LNet support for PCI P2P DMA"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Venkata Ravi Theja Reddy Venuthurla",
          "email": "venkata.ravi.theja.reddy.venu@oracle.com",
          "date": "2026-08-31 15:45:07.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Venkata Ravi Theja Reddy Venuthurla",
          "email": "venkata.ravi.theja.reddy.venu@oracle.com",
          "date": "2026-09-02 15:04:39.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "subject": "LU-20680 socklnd: order delayed receive state publication",
        "message": "LU-20680 socklnd: order delayed receive state publication\n\nlnet_parse() may invoke ksocknal_recv() asynchronously while\nksocknal_process_receive() waits for it to provide the receive tuple.\nksocknal_recv() initializes the tuple before changing ksnc_rx_state\nto SOCKNAL_RX_LNET_PAYLOAD, but the scheduler reads that state without\nholding kss_lock.\n\nOn weakly ordered CPUs, the scheduler can observe RX_LNET_PAYLOAD\nbefore the associated receive tuple becomes visible, leaving its\niterator empty and triggering an assertion.\n\nPublish RX_LNET_PAYLOAD with release semantics and consume it with an\nacquire load. This makes the fully initialized receive tuple visible\nwhenever the scheduler observes the payload state.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Venkata Ravi Theja Reddy Venuthurla <venkata.ravi.theja.reddy.venu@oracle.com>\nChange-Id: Idf677a496ba656e850aca754b20b1ec57fda6024\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
